-# Native GC integration: current ABI1 comparison path
+# Native GC integration
+
+## ABI2 fixed reservation and refusal diagnostics
+
+The current ABI2 collector reserves one fixed 512 MiB virtual heap window.
+The nursery/control boundary remains at 8 MiB and large-object space remains
+128 MiB, beginning at 384 MiB, so demand-paged small-object old space is
+376 MiB. The larger reservation does not eagerly commit its additional
+address range. Compact offsets remain below the bit-31 forwarding tag, and the
+packed LOS owner/extent representation still covers exactly 32,768 pages.
+
+All heap-indexed start, mark, pending, block, descriptor, dirty-card and
+free-block metadata offsets derive from the reserved window. `N_STARTS=65536`
+and the assembly-visible control prefix remain stable. `ng_open` rejects a
+layout whose forwarding, partition-alignment, ordering or 64 MiB metadata
+bounds do not hold. Generated subtype tests and single/range card barriers use
+the same exported layout constants as the collector.
+
+Collection admission is otherwise unchanged: relocation starts only after
+credit covers promotion bytes plus one block per active worker and the
+largest-object loss in every run. The bounded 65,536-run table, age census,
+survivor bounds, ownership, process-wide worker lease and poison-on-partial-
+trace behavior remain intact.
+
+Unused control-prefix cells record the last attempt without worker-side
+telemetry. Attempt kinds are minor (1), major (2), allocation (3), and root
+publication (4); results are success (1), refused (2), and poisoned (3).
+Stable first-cause refusal IDs are old credit (1), run table (2), page protect
+(3), root table (4), borrow/mode (5), poison (6), LOS capacity (7), and internal
+trace/state failure (8). Each new attempt clears the prior reason. Admission
+also records need, available credit, run count, promotion bytes, largest object
+and worker count. Allocation failure output includes these fields; successful
+retry cannot inherit a stale refusal.
+
+True exhaustion remains fail-closed. A failed minor preflight leaves roots,
+cards and object headers retryable; the runtime performs its existing bounded
+major-plus-minor retry and then returns the same runtime-allocation trap. Map,
+run, root, LOS and internal failures remain separately diagnosable. No mapping
+is moved or resized while helpers or generated code can observe it.
+
+## Historical ABI1 comparison path
 
